This is 99% invisible. I'm Roman Mars. This summer, the governors of New Mexico and Colorado got into a fight on Twitter. Words were had, umbridge was taken, but the fight wasn't over tax incentives or highway funding or water rights. Instead, it all boiled down to this. Colorado's governor had the gall to insult New Mexico's pride and joy. It's chili peppers.
这里是“99%隐形”。我是罗曼·马斯。今年夏天，新墨西哥州和科罗拉多州的州长在推特上大打口水战。双方唇枪舌剑，互不相让，但这场争端无关税收优惠、高速公路资金或水权。归根结底，原因只有一个。科罗拉多州州长竟然大言不惭地侮辱了新墨西哥州的骄傲与灵魂——辣椒。

