New Mexicans like June have been growing their own varieties for over a hundred years. Mostly unsmall family farms that remain dedicated to this one beloved crop for generations. But despite these growers pride in their peppers, all is not well in Miss Juni's kingdom. New Mexico's chili may be the best in the world, but for a while now, the chili business has been in trouble. New Mexico chili farmers have a problem, one that might soon force them to choose between tradition and technology. When I started reporting this story,
像琼这样的新墨西哥州人培育自己的品种已经有一百多年了。这些大多是小型家庭农场，世世代代专注种植这唯一的挚爱作物。但尽管这些种植者对自己的辣椒充满骄傲，“小琼”的王国里并非一帆风顺。新墨西哥州的辣椒可能是世界上最好的，但一段时间以来，辣椒产业一直陷入困境。新墨西哥州的辣椒农面临着一个问题，这个问题可能很快迫使他们在传统与技术之间做出抉择。当我开始报道这个故事时，

