00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Glen runs a chili farm called Five Star Chili in Sacoro, New Mexico. And he says that every year things get a little more bleak for the business. It's not that nobody wants to buy chili. Nationwide demand for chili peppers is at an all-time high. And yet, the economics of being a chili farmer, they're just not working out. It's been wild this year. It was bad weather, but it's more than that. It's like the perfect storm came together.
格伦在新墨西哥州索科罗经营着一家名为“五星辣椒”的辣椒农场。他说，这个行业的情况每年都在变得更加黯淡。并不是没有人想买辣椒。全国对辣椒的需求处于历史最高水平。然而，作为一名辣椒农的经济账，却怎么也算不过来。今年简直太疯狂了。天气很糟，但原因不止于此。这就好像是一场完美的风暴聚在了一起。

