problem. There just aren't enough workers to pick the peppers. We hire everybody that comes up, everybody. When I visited Glenn's farm, he had eight workers out in the field, picking chiles. He says on a good year in the past, he would have had 30, mostly from Mexico. They would go to one ranch house, work a few days for them, they would feed them, take care of them, and this and that, and go to the next ranch house, and they would eventually get here. That hasn't happened in years.
根本没有足够的工人来采摘辣椒。我们把来应聘的人全招了，所有人都是。当我参观格伦的农场时，他有八个工人在地里采摘辣椒。他说，在过去的一个好年景里，他会雇30个人，大部分来自墨西哥。他们会去一个农庄，为他们干几天活，农庄管饭、照顾他们诸如此云，然后再去下一个农庄，最后他们总能来到这里。这种情况已经多年没有发生了。

