00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:48.000
It's not just Glenn, and it's not just the Chile industry. Farms across the United States are reporting shortages of labor. Since 2002, the number of immigrants coming to the United States to work in agriculture has dropped by 75%. In California, one survey found that 56% of farmers were unable to hire enough workers. The number of people immigrating to the US for farm labor has actually been going down since 2008, like when the economy crashed here. That's Sarah Taber, a crop scientist based in Fayetteville, North Carolina.
不只是格伦，也不只是辣椒产业。全美各地的农场都在报告劳动力短缺。自2002年以来，来到美国从事农业劳工的移民数量下降了75%。在加利福尼亚州，一项调查发现，56%的农场主无法雇到足够的工人。事实上，为了从事农业劳动力而移民美国的人数自2008年以来一直在下降，就像当年这里的经济崩溃时一样。这是常驻北卡罗来纳州费耶特维尔的农作物科学家莎拉·泰伯说的。

