It's not even that this work doesn't pay well. It does. Farm laborers in New Mexico's chili fields can make double the state's minimum wage. They can make nearly twice as much picking chili as they could working at a chili's restaurant. But they still don't want to do it. In part because picking chili peppers can be especially grueling work, even compared to other crops. Chili plants grow low to the ground, and the chilis themselves often sit close to the stem nestled deep inside the bush.
甚至不是因为这项工作报酬不好。其实挺不错的。新墨西哥州辣椒田里的农业工人的工资可以达到该州最低工资的两倍。他们采摘辣椒的收入几乎是在辣椒餐厅（Chili's）打工的两倍。但他们依然不愿意干。部分原因在于，即便与其他农作物相比，采摘辣椒也是一项格外折磨人的艰苦工作。辣椒植株长得很矮，辣椒本身往往紧贴着主茎，深深地隐藏在灌木丛深处。

