So workers have to hunch over in the hot sun to get them. All this while wearing gloves to protect their hands from the oils that give chilies their characteristic heat. And green chili peppers, the kind of gland and a lot of other New Mexico chili farmers rely on, are especially hard to pick. Green chilies are just unripe red chilies, which means that the seeds inside of them aren't ready to germinate yet. The plant doesn't want to give its fruits up, so its stems won't let go without a fight.
因此，工人们必须在烈日下弯腰驼背才能摘到辣椒。与此同时，他们还得戴着手套，以保护双手免受辣椒素的侵扰，正是这种油脂赋予了辣椒标志性的辣味。而青辣椒——格伦和许多其他新墨西哥州辣椒农所依赖的品种——格外难以采摘。青辣椒只是未成熟的红辣椒，这意味着它们内部的种子还没有准备好发芽。植物不想放弃它的果实，所以它的茎部不经过一番较量是绝不会松手的。

